# A permission ask, refused with Esc, then asked again and allowed with Enter (the dialog's first
# choice, Yes, is the one selected): the first turn is interrupted and the second finishes, as in
# tests/fixtures/claude-hooks/tui-perm-*.log. A command that sets a variable is not one claude's
# sandbox lets run unasked. Two prompts.
agent claude-code
recording tui-perm
timeout 180
expect interrupted finished

sleep 5
press down
press enter
wait-for SessionStart
sleep 2
type run exactly this shell command: FOO=bar ls
press enter
wait-for PermissionRequest
sleep 2
press esc
sleep 3
type run exactly this shell command again: FOO=bar ls
press enter
wait-for PermissionRequest
sleep 2
press enter
wait-for Stop
